# Secrets & security

- NEVER commit secrets or API keys. Use `.env` files; provide `.env.example` with placeholder values.
- Keep `.env`, `google-services*.json`, and `google-service-account.json` git-ignored.
- Credentials live only in env/config:
  - `backend/.env` — MongoDB/Redis credentials, JWT secret, admin bootstrap login, CORS, Firebase service account (optional; push only), Google/Facebook OAuth ids. No SMTP, no payment-provider secret.
  - `Admin Dashboard/.env` — `VITE_*` (server URLs, Cloudinary upload folders, Firebase push).
  - `CustomerApp/.env` — `GRAPHQL_URL`, `WS_GRAPHQL_URL`, Stripe publishable key, Google OAuth, Amplitude. (No maps/location keys — the app has no maps dependency.)
- The Stripe **secret** key (`sk_*`) must never live in env or in a client app: it is saved through the admin `saveStripeConfiguration` mutation and stored in the DB. Only the publishable key (`pk_*`) goes in `CustomerApp/.env`.
- Do not introduce new hardcoded keys when refactoring.
- A pre-tool-use hook (`secret-guard.cjs`) blocks writing known secret patterns; honor it and move the value to `.env` instead.
